mundane theorem subset-antisymmetric
  note        Two sets each a part of the other are one set: each inclusion
              says every member of one is in the other, which is what the
              axiom of extensionality asks.
  let X be a set                                                      (H1)
  let Y be a set                                                      (H2)
  assume X ⊆ Y                                                        (H3)
  assume Y ⊆ X                                                        (H4)
  then X = Y

1.  For all t ∈ X, t ∈ Y.
    mun:subset, from H3

2.  For all t ∈ Y, t ∈ X.
    mun:subset X := Y, Y := X, from H4

3.  X = Y
    axi:extensionality, from 1, 2
